icinga-sso-web (1:1.0.0+imatic6) icinga; urgency=medium

  * Return a proper 400 for an external post-login redirect, as Icinga Web's
    own AuthenticationController does, instead of the silent dashboard
    fallback added in +imatic5. The fallback was only needed because the error
    page could not render: Auth::setAuthenticated() does not set the user on
    the request, so AutoRefreshForm hit a null user. Set the user on the
    request too — mirroring EmbeddedWeb::setupUser() — and let LoginRedirect
    reject the URL as core intends.

 -- Anima Artificialis <anima.artificialis@gmail.com>  Thu, 08 Oct 2026 16:39:50 +0000

icinga-sso-web (1:1.0.0+imatic5) icinga; urgency=medium

  * Do not let LoginRedirect's HttpBadRequestException escape the OIDC
    callback. The user is authenticated by that point, but setAuthenticated()
    does not put the user on the request, so Icinga's error page itself fatals
    in AutoRefreshForm (getRequest()->getUser() is null) and the browser gets
    an uncaught Error instead of a 400. Catch it, log the refused target, and
    fall back to the dashboard — the external redirect is refused either way.

 -- Anima Artificialis <anima.artificialis@gmail.com>  Thu, 08 Oct 2026 16:15:04 +0000

icinga-sso-web (1:1.0.0+imatic4) icinga; urgency=medium

  * Rebase onto upstream main (abff75c), picking up "Keep the refresh token if
    the IdP doesn't rotate it" (#18) — relevant for providers that omit the
    refresh token on reauth, as RFC 6749 section 6 permits.
  * Document the raised requirement: Icinga Web >= 2.14, matching the
    dependency bump from +imatic3.

 -- Anima Artificialis <anima.artificialis@gmail.com>  Thu, 08 Oct 2026 12:43:34 +0000

icinga-sso-web (1:1.0.0+imatic3) icinga; urgency=medium

  * Require icingaweb2 (>= 2.14.0). The LoginRedirect element introduced in
    +imatic2 only exists from Icinga Web 2.14.0; the inherited (>= 2.13.0)
    dependency let the package install on 2.13.x, where the SSO callback then
    died on a missing class after a successful authentication.

 -- Anima Artificialis <anima.artificialis@gmail.com>  Thu, 08 Oct 2026 12:36:09 +0000

icinga-sso-web (1:1.0.0+imatic2) icinga; urgency=medium

  * Use Icinga Web's core LoginRedirect element for the post-login redirect
    (follow-up to upstream review on PR #13). Adds the fallback to
    LoginForm::REDIRECT_URL and the guard against redirecting back to
    authentication/logout.
  * Behaviour change: an external redirect URL now raises HttpBadRequestException
    instead of silently falling back to the dashboard, matching the core login.

 -- Anima Artificialis <anima.artificialis@gmail.com>  Thu, 08 Oct 2026 12:22:50 +0000

icinga-sso-web (1:1.0.0+imatic1) icinga; urgency=medium

  * Unofficial patched rebuild of icinga-sso-web 1.0.0.
  * Add post-login OIDC redirect fix (icinga-sso-web PR #13): after SSO sign-in
    redirect to the originally requested URL instead of always the dashboard;
    external URLs rejected via Url::fromPath()->isExternal().
  * Epoch bump (1:) so this drop-in supersedes the official 1.0.0 package and
    its nightly snapshots on upgrade.

